### Recommended practices

- Use plain, direct language.
- Keep messages focused on one topic.
- State the requested action explicitly.
- Include the deadline and time zone.
- Avoid unexplained acronyms and idioms.
- Use bullets, headings and examples.
- Separate facts, assumptions and opinions.
- Confirm interpretation of ambiguous points.
- Summarize complex verbal discussions in writing.
- Avoid sarcasm, humor or indirect wording when the meaning may be unclear.

Instead of:

> “Can we try to get this sorted fairly soon?”

Use:

> “Please confirm by 15:00 UTC on Thursday whether the API change can be completed for the 20 June release. If not, identify the earliest achievable date and the resulting impact.”

